course: dictionary
lesson: 2526
title: Many meanings of one word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Decorate means to make something look nicer by adding pretty things to it. A baker decorates a cake with icing, and a family decorates a tree for a festival.
explain: Decorate has a second meaning: to paint walls or put up wallpaper in a room. This meaning is used mostly in the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand. Context tells you which meaning is right: «We decorated the bedroom in pale green» is about paint, not about pretty things.
explain: Decorate can also mean to give someone a medal or honour. «The soldier was decorated for bravery» means he was given a medal for being brave, not that he was painted. Always try your meaning in the sentence. Does «the soldier was given a medal for bravery» still make sense? Then you have found the right meaning.
fact: Decorate means to make something look nicer by adding pretty things.
fact: «Pysanky» are Ukrainian Easter eggs decorated with wax and dye, with patterns like the sun, wheat or waves.
fact: «Van Gogh» painted sunflower pictures in 1888 and 1889 to decorate a room for his friend, the painter Paul Gauguin.
fact: «The Assyrians» built great palaces at Nineveh, decorated with stone pictures of lion hunts.
fact: Decorate can also mean to give someone a medal or honour, as in «the soldier was decorated for bravery».
exercise: «Pysanky are Ukrainian Easter eggs decorated with wax and dye.» What does decorated mean here? | Broken into pieces | Hidden under the ground | Left plain and empty | *Made to look nicer with patterns
exercise: Which sentence uses decorate to mean paint or wallpaper a room? | «The tree was decorated with silver stars.» | *«We decorated the living room in pale green.» | «The cake was decorated with pink icing.» | «The soldier was decorated for bravery.»
exercise: «The soldier was decorated for bravery.» What was he given? | *A medal for being brave | A new coat | A ticket to the zoo | Ten pounds from the shop
test: «Van Gogh painted sunflowers to decorate a room for his friend.» What does decorate mean here? | To knock the walls down | To leave the room empty | *To make the room look nicer | To move house
test: Mum says, «We are decorating the bedroom this weekend.» What is she planning? | To sleep in the bedroom | To clean the windows | To buy a new bed | *To paint the walls or put up wallpaper
exam: Mo says decorate only means to paint a room. Why is he wrong? | Decorate means to dig a hole | Decorate means to break things | He is right, there is only one meaning | *Decorate can also mean making things look pretty or giving someone a medal
